# PLACA client environment variables
#
# Vite loads this file from the client/ directory when running the dev server
# or a build. Copy it before running the client without Docker:
#
#   cp client/.env.example client/.env
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to browser code. Never put a
# secret here: anything VITE_* is embedded in the built JavaScript.
#
# With Docker Compose the root .env is passed to the client container instead,
# so this file is only needed when running the client directly.

# ---------- API ----------
# Base URL for API requests. Leave blank to use the relative /api path, which
# goes through the Vite dev proxy locally and nginx in production. Set an
# absolute URL only when the API lives on another origin; add this site's
# origin to CORS_ORIGINS on the server.
#
# Example for a Vercel client with a Render API:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://placa-project.onrender.com/api
#   SITE_URL=https://placa-project.vercel.app
#
# Vercel does not read this file from git (it is ignored). Add both variables in
# the Vercel project's Environment Variables settings and redeploy.
VITE_API_URL=

# Where the Vite dev server proxies /api. Not used by production builds.
VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5000

# ---------- Public site metadata (build only, not browser code) ----------
# Optional absolute public address. When set, canonical/hreflang/og:url become
# absolute and dist/sitemap.xml is generated. Leave blank to keep relative URLs.
SITE_URL=
